Archived code from the earlier ncurses-based nano port of gano.

gano-main.scm was the top-level gano.scm; it `include`s the files that
lived in src/ (now in this directory), so it will not run from here as-is.

gano/ holds superseded versions of the character buffer:
  cbuf.scm             - the monolithic (gano cbuf) module, replaced by
                         cbuf-core / cbuf-basic / cbuf-standard / cbuf-extra
  cbuf2.scm            - notes/snippets merged into cbuf-basic
  cbuf-ops.scm,
  cbuf-operations.scm  - two drafts that both declared (gano cbuf-operations)

The old test suite is in ../old-test.

uax9-*.scm (gano/) and their tests (../old-test/test-uax9-*.scm,
test-text-metrics-bidi.scm) are a UAX #9 bidirectional algorithm that
reordered cell positions visually.  That was the wrong model: terminals
do their own bidi reordering of the logical text they are sent.  Bidi
support is postponed; gano currently lays all text out left to right.
